# Tangerine Compiler — Semantic Edit Protocol (audit item 53)
# Self-hosting compiler written in Tangerine
#
# The typed SEMANTIC EDIT protocol: one SemanticEdit request is RESOLVED
# against the §32 read-side index / §29 snapshot (the typed stable ids —
# StableDeclId / StableRowKey / the canonical contract and call row keys —
# are the resolution authority) and then APPLIED on the tractable surface
# the representation actually exposes. The protocol never edits text: a
# resolved edit carries the canonical target keys, the dependency-closure
# affected set and the resolved preconditions; the apply step either
# produces a real semantic artifact (the ChangeContract snapshot + §31
# delta; the FillHole typed-node patch) or returns the typed
# EditError::ApplyUnavailable with the exact remaining surface named by
# semantic_edit_unavailable_reason — never a marker token, never a silent
# no-op.
#
# MODEL MAPPING (what each edit resolves against, and what applies):
#
#   Rename(decl, new_name)
#     resolve — the StableDeclId of `decl` through the snapshot's symbol
#       rows (an exact full stable key, or a bare / qualified NAME that must
#       be unique — two matches are EditError::AmbiguousTarget), then the
#       direct callers via the §32 index (index_callers_of_decl over the
#       re-derived StableDeclId) and the FULL affected set via the §31
#       affected_closure over the default kinds.
#     apply — REAL on the source surface (third-audit item 30): the
#       declaration named by the resolved stable key is renamed on the
#       parsed AST and every identifier / type / path occurrence whose text
#       matches the old name is rewritten (the stable rows re-key through
#       the caller pipeline); the edited tree is rendered by the formatter
#       and re-validated. The snapshot-only apply_edit entry still answers
#       ApplyUnavailable (no source rides it) with the source entry named.
#
#   ChangeSignature(decl, new_signature_text)
#     resolve — the same declaration resolution; the CALL SITES THAT MUST
#       UPDATE are counted from the index's reverse call graph and ride the
#       preconditions ("callsites-to-update:<n>") — the resolved fact the
#       audit asks for.
#     apply — REAL (declaration side, source surface): the replacement
#       signature text is parsed and spliced (name/generics/params/return/
#       where clause) on the parsed AST, rendered and re-validated; call
#       site updates are NOT auto-performed in this slice — the resolved
#       affected set / "callsites-to-update:<n>" precondition carries them
#       and the apply row records "callsites-not-updated:<n>". The
#       snapshot-only apply_edit entry answers ApplyUnavailable.
#
#   ChangeContract(contract_id, new_expression_text)
#     resolve — the contract ROW by its StableContractId.stable_key (the
#       canonical "<fn key>|Pre|Post|Invariant|<clause>" text) in the
#       snapshot's contracts table; the function is the row's subject and
#       the affected closure is seeded with it.
#     apply — REAL: parse the new canonical "op(arg,...)" text, rebuild the
#       ContractFact (canonical_expression + expression_fingerprint + the
#       re-keyed StableContractId), copy the snapshot, and diff
#       before/after with semantic_delta_of — the returned
#       EditApplication carries the updated snapshot AND the actual §31
#       delta (the Removed old-key + Created new-key contract_delta rows
#       are the proof of application, exactly as the re-keyed identity
#       demands). A malformed canonical text is
#       EditError::PreconditionFailed.
#
#   ReplaceCall(call_site_key, callee)
#     resolve — the call ROW by its canonical "caller|callee|kind" key
#       (stable_row_key domain "call" + the table scan against CallEdge
#       rows), the new callee key (must resolve), the caller and the
#       affected closure seeded with the caller.
#     apply — REAL on the source surface (third-audit item 30): every
#       direct call site in the caller's body whose callee name matches the
#       old callee is replaced with the new callee (bare name or qualified
#       path) on the parsed AST, rendered and re-validated; a call row
#       whose kind is not Direct is PreconditionFailed (its callee is not a
#       source name). The snapshot-only apply_edit entry answers
#       ApplyUnavailable.
#
#   InsertStatement(function_key, before_stmt_key, statement_text)
#     resolve — the function's symbol row, the §33 statement key's prefix
#       (it must belong to the function: "<fn key>#B..."), and the affected
#       closure seeded with the function.
#     apply — REAL on the source surface (third-audit item 30): the
#       statement text is parsed and spliced before the mapped anchor —
#       top-level body block B0 at statement ordinal S<idx>; a non-zero
#       block, an out-of-range ordinal, a non-block body or an unparsable
#       statement text is PreconditionFailed (the evidence detail names the
#       reason; the §33 anchor is MIR-derived, so the mapping is bounded
#       and documented). The snapshot-only apply_edit entry answers
#       ApplyUnavailable.
#
#   FillHole(hole_key, expression_text)
#     resolve — the canonical hole key "<fn stable key>#hole<node id>"
#       (semantic_hole_key_of / semantic_hole_key_parts); the function
#       prefix resolves through the symbol rows and the affected closure is
#       seeded with it. The hole's TYPED constraints are read through
#       types.tg's hole_constraints_of / typed_hole_constraints_of (the
#       node id is part of the key).
#     apply — REAL on the typed-program patch surface:
#       apply_fill_hole(inout program: TypedProgram, resolved, replacement)
#       verifies the node carries TypedExprKind::Hole and replaces it with
#       the checker-produced TypedExpr. The expression TEXT cannot be
#       parsed+checked here (the checker env is not part of the patch
#       surface), so the edit carries the text and the caller supplies the
#       typed form — that is the honest split the representation permits.
#       apply_edit(snapshot, ...) answers ApplyUnavailable for FillHole with
#       the pointer to apply_fill_hole.
#
# DEFAULT CLOSURE KINDS: the data-bearing DependencyEdgeKind classes (Call /
# EffectPropagation / CapabilityPropagation / Implements / ContainsType /
# AbiConsumer / ContractReferences / TestReferences). The no-row families
# (GenericInstantiation / LayoutDependent / ConstEvalDependent /
# DerivedImpl) are covered by the call closure anyway, so omitting them
# loses no traversal (see affected_closure's per-kind data matrix).
#
# DETERMINISM: every resolved row set is sorted by the closure / accessor
# that produced it; the apply result rows are canonical texts. No env
# gates.
#
# (third-audit item 30) THE SOURCE REWRITE ENGINE: the edits above whose
# apply used to end at ApplyUnavailable now APPLY for real on source text.
# edit_apply_to_source(source, resolved) transforms the PARSED AST
# (Rename: declaration + every matching identifier/type/path occurrence;
# ReplaceCall: every direct call site of the caller's body; InsertStatement:
# a statement spliced before the mapped §33 anchor; ChangeSignature: the
# declaration's signature splice) and renders the edited tree through the
# canonical formatter; apply_edit_to_source then re-validates the
# regenerated source (parse -> resolve -> type -> access -> ownership) and
# returns the EditApplication record (edited_source + validation status +
# the expected delta rows) the caller's
# SemanticSnapshot' -> SemanticDelta -> ChangeBudget -> ProofCarryingPatch
# pipeline consumes. The snapshot-level apply_edit entry keeps its
# existing behavior for callers that hold no source (Rename etc. still
# answer ApplyUnavailable there, with the source entry named).

use std::core::{Option, Result}
use std::collections::{Vec}

